{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Information.SkeinShadowConjInvariance","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Information.SkeinShadowConjInvariance","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Information.SkeinObservationBridge","lean:module:QOU.Information.MagnitudeTraceCommutator"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.trace_obs_collapses_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.trace_obs_collapses_conj","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinShadowConjInvariance.lean#L70-L80","doc":"**The concrete collapse hypothesis for `obs = tr_M` is `M ∘ Q = M`\n(sorry-free).**  When the observation is the Markov trace, the relabeling the\nshadow is blind to is conjugation `conjOp u`, and the `hobs` hypothesis above\nis exactly `MagnitudeTraceCommutator.magnitude_trace_conj`.  This grounds the\nabstract lossy-shadow lemma in the operator lemma — the trace shadow's\nconjugation-blindness is not assumed but proved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.haltsObserved_relabel_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.haltsObserved_relabel_iff","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinShadowConjInvariance.lean#L54-L68","doc":"**The trace-shadow is lossy (sorry-free).**  `HaltsObserved` cannot\ndistinguish a state from its relabel: `HaltsObserved (τ P) ↔ HaltsObserved P`\nwhenever `τ` is obs-collapsed and step-equivariant.  Since `Halts` is *not*\n`τ`-invariant in general, this is precisely the failed converse of\n`haltsObserved_of_halts` — the observation is easy (blind to `τ`) while the\ndynamics is hard (sees `τ`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.obs_iterate_relabel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.obs_iterate_relabel","kind":"theorem","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/SkeinShadowConjInvariance.lean#L38-L52","doc":"**The observed orbit is invariant under an obs-collapsed, step-equivariant\nrelabeling (sorry-free).**  If `τ` commutes with `step` and `obs` collapses\nit (`obs ∘ τ = obs`), then `obs (stepᵏ (τ x)) = obs (stepᵏ x)` for every `k`\n— the observation reads `τ`-conjugate states identically at every stage. ","signatureChunk":0}]}